From: the jellyfin-ffmpeg contributors
Subject: add vendor id option for d3d11
Origin: https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg/blob/v8.1.3-2/debian/patches/0013-add-vendor-id-option-for-d3d11.patch

`vendor=` picks the D3D11 adapter as `vendor_id=` does: the name
commands written for jellyfin-ffmpeg use.

Rebased onto FFmpeg 9.0.2: the same change, at 9.0.2's line numbers.

From jellyfin-ffmpeg 8.1.3-2, where the patch has no header: its authors
are in that repository's history. Under FFmpeg's licence, as the files
it changes.
---
diff --git a/libavutil/hwcontext_d3d11va.c b/libavutil/hwcontext_d3d11va.c
--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_d3d11va.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_d3d11va.c
@@ -644,6 +644,8 @@ static int d3d11va_device_create(AVHWDev
         adapter = atoi(device);
     } else {
         AVDictionaryEntry *e = av_dict_get(opts, "vendor_id", NULL, 0);
+        if (!e || !e->value)
+            e = av_dict_get(opts, "vendor", NULL, 0); // for backward compatibility
         if (e && e->value) {
             adapter = d3d11va_device_find_adapter_by_vendor_id(ctx, creationFlags, e->value);
             if (adapter < 0) {
